- Map the tooling ecosystem an MLE works with daily: ML frameworks, experiment tracking (MLflow, W&B), MLOps platforms (Kubeflow, SageMaker, Vertex AI), data tools (Spark, dbt), model serving (Triton, TorchServe, vLLM), monitoring, and cloud infrastructure
- Research relevant codebases (using Bitbucket/Github search) to understand existing ML infrastructure patterns — model serving architecture, training pipelines, inference optimization, and how ML code is structured in production systems
- Define the technical domain expertise required: NLP/LLM fine-tuning, computer vision, recommendation systems, reinforcement learning, or other specializations relevant to the startup's product
</UserRequest>

