## 4. Relevant Codebase Patterns from Production Systems

### 4.1 ML Studio Module Architecture (Monorepo)
The `ml-studio` Bitbucket repository is a centralized ML module monorepo containing **65+ training modules across 20+ teams**:

```
ml-studio/
├── modules/src/
│   ├── ai_modeling/          # HSTU, recommendation models
│   ├── search_relevance/     # L2 rankers, two-tower models, multitask learning
│   ├── knowledge_graph/      # Jira L2 ranker, entity models
│   ├── ai_assistant/         # Intent classifier, LLaMA Factory fine-tuning
│   ├── ml_platform/          # LLM fine-tune modules, ML Fabric orchestration
│   ├── loom_ai/              # Audio/speech synthesis models
│   ├── confluence_ai/        # Prompt suggestion models
│   └── canary_analysis/      # Deployment anomaly detection
├── workflows/                # YAML workflow descriptors
└── module_descriptor.yaml     # Module metadata and versioning
```

### 4.2 Training Pipeline Pattern (GPU-Accelerated)
```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  ML Studio Workflow (YAML)              │
│  - Orchestrates data prep + training    │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
                ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│Module1: Data Preparation (Spark)     │
│  - Feature engineering, train/val split │
│  - Save to Databricks Volumes│
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
                    ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Module 2: GPU Training (ML Fabric)     │
│  - Multi-GPU distributed (DDP)          │
│  - Track with MLflow                    │
│  - Save model artifacts                 │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
                    ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Module 3: Evaluation + Registration│
│  - Quality gate checks                  │
│  - Register to ML Registry (Tarot)      │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### 4.3 Model Serving Architecture (Triton)
```
<model_name>/
├── config.pbtxt          # Triton model config (backend, batching, instance_group)
├── 1/# Version directory
│   ├── model.py# Triton Python backend (initialize, execute, finalize)
│   ├── model.onnx       # ONNX weights
│   └── tokenizer files  # tokenizer.json, config.json
```

**Traffic flow for inference:**
```
Internet (HTTPS)
    ↓
AWS ALB (TLS Termination, Port 443)
    ↓
Istio Gateway (Protocol Routing)
    ↓
VirtualService (Path-based Routing)
    ↓
DestinationRule (LEAST_REQUEST Load Balancing)
    ↓
Model Pods (TensorRT-LLM, Triton, vLLM)
```

### 4.4 Feature Engineering Pipeline Pattern
```python
# Tecton DSL feature definition
@batch_feature_view(
    sources=[socrates_events_source],
    entities=[user],
    mode="batch",
    aggregations=[
        Aggregation(column="score", function="avg", time_window="1d"),
    ],
    ttl="30d"
)
def user_engagement_features(events_df):
    return events_df[["id", "score", "created_at"]]
```

**Data flow:**
```
User Interactions → Plato (Kafka) → Databricks → Tecton Feature Store
                                                    ├── Online (DynamoDB) → Real-time inference
                                                    └── Offline (S3/Delta) → Model training
```

### 4.5 LLM Fine-Tuning Pipeline (Production Pattern)
```yaml
# Multi-stage LoRA fine-tuning workflow
name: qwen25-14b-multistage-lora-ft
module_tasks:
  - step_name: data_preparation
    module: mlp_prepare_llm_fine_tune_datasets
    parameters:
      - name: datasets_config
        value: "task: sft\ndatasets:\n  - dataset_name: HuggingFaceH4/ultrachat_200k"- step_name: train
    module: mlp_llm_finetune
    platform_override: "fabric"  # Use ML Fabric GPU cluster
    parameters:
      - name: base_model_uri
        value: hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct
      - name: file__training_config.yaml
        value: |
          stage: sft
          finetuning_type: lora
          lora_rank: 16
          quantization_bit: 4
          deepspeed: ds_z2_config.json
          gradient_checkpointing: true
```

### 4.6 PyTorch Model Patterns in Production

**Deep learning models in production** (from ML Studio modules):
| Model Type | Architecture | Key Patterns |
|------------|-------------|--------------|
| Sequential Recommendation (HSTU) | 6custom `nn.Module` subclasses, causal masking, ~30M-item embeddings | AdamW, parameter freezing for DDP |
| Multitask L2 Ranking | DCN + embeddings, task-specific heads | BCELoss, gradient accumulation |
| Two-tower Embedding | BERT + MLP variants with shared encoders | Separate trainer classes, task-specific projections |
| Generative (Speech/Audio) | Flow-matching denoising, PyTorch Lightning | Masked MSE loss, conditional generation |
| Intent Classification | Fine-tuned transformer + PEFT | Lightning-based trainer with callbacks |

