## 2. Required Technical Skills with Competency Levels

### 2.1 Competency Level Framework (Aligned to Atlassian P40–P60)

| Dimension | P40 (Mid-Level) | P50 (Senior) | P60 (Principal/Staff) |
|-----------|-----------------|--------------|----------------------|
| Experience | ~2–4 years ML industry | ~4–8 years | ~9–14+ years |
| Scope | Build production ML models independently | Lead small team, own mid-to-large projects | End-to-end technical leadership, cross-org influence |
| Engineering/ML Split | 70% engineering / 30% ML | 60/40 balanced | Strategic + deep specialization |

### 2.2 Deep Learning Frameworks

| Skill | P40 | P50 | P60 |
|-------|-----|-----|-----|
| **PyTorch** | Custom `nn.Module`, train/eval loops, DataLoaders | DDP distributed training, custom optimizers, mixed precision | Multi-node training, custom kernels, operator fusion |
| **JAX** | Basic usage, functional programming patterns | XLA compilation, TPU utilization | Custom training loops, Flax/Haiku architectures at scale |
| **TensorFlow** | Keras API, TF Serving integration | TensorRT optimization, distributed strategies | TF-TensorRT compilation, production pipeline design |
| **HuggingFace** | Transformers library, tokenizers, model loading | Trainer API, PEFT/LoRA, Accelerate | Custom architectures, multi-stage training orchestration |

### 2.3 Classical ML & Statistical Methods

| Skill | P40 | P50 | P60 |
|-------|-----|-----|-----|
| **Tree-based models** | XGBoost, LightGBM training and evaluation | Feature importance, hyperparameter optimization, LTR models | Architecture decisions on when classical beats deep |
| **Statistical methods** | Hypothesis testing, A/B test analysis | Bayesian inference, causal modeling | Advanced experimentation design, multi-armed bandits |
| **Data processing** | Pandas, NumPy, basic PySpark | Large-scale Spark pipelines, streaming | Distributed system design, data architecture |

### 2.4 Distributed Training & Infrastructure

| Skill | P40 | P50 | P60 |
|-------|-----|-----|-----|
| **Distributed training** | Single-node multi-GPU with DDP | Multi-node with torchrun, DeepSpeed ZeRO | Training at10B+ parameter scale, sharding strategies, FSDP |
| **Cloud infrastructure** | Basic AWS/GCP usage | SageMaker, EKS/GKE, capacity planning | Multi-cloud strategy, TPU/GPU allocation optimization |
| **Containerization** | Docker basics, environment management | Docker for ML workflows, Kubernetes jobs | ML Fabric architecture, Kueue scheduling, gang scheduling |

### 2.5 Model Optimization (Quantization, Distillation, Pruning)

| Skill | P40 | P50 | P60 |
|-------|-----|-----|-----|
| **Quantization** | INT8/INT4basics, bitsandbytes usage | GPTQ, AWQ, mixed precision training (bf16) | TensorRT compilation, custom calibration, production quantization pipelines |
| **LoRA/PEFT** | Basic LoRA fine-tuning (rank 8–16) | Multi-stageLoRA, QLoRA, adapter merging | Multi-LoRA serving, adapter orchestration at scale |
| **Knowledge distillation** | Teacher-student basics | Teacher logit extraction, quality gates | Distillation pipeline design, cost-quality tradeoff optimization |
| **Pruning** | Basic magnitude pruning | Structured pruning, sparsity-aware training | Custom pruning strategies for production constraints |

### 2.6 Software Engineering Fundamentals

| Skill | P40 | P50 | P60 |
|-------|-----|-----|-----|
| **Production code** | Python production-quality, test-driven | Code reviews, documentation, architecture design | System-level architecture, cross-team patterns |
| **CI/CD** | Basic pipelines, unit tests | ML-specific CI/CD, integration testing | MLOps pipeline design, continuous training automation |
| **Languages** | Python (primary), SQL | + Java/Kotlin, Go | Polyglot, performance-critical code in C++ |
| **System design** | RESTful APIs, microservices basics | Distributed systems, event-driven architecture | Platform-level design, multi-region architecture |

