# MLE Operational Framework: Domain Artifacts, Collaboration Patterns, Metrics, Failure Modes, and Organizational Integration

## 1. Domain Operational Artifacts an MLE Produces and Maintains

### Model Registry Artifacts
At Atlassian, the **ML Registry (Tarot)** is the central source of truth for all registered models. MLEs produce and maintain:

- **Model Artifacts**: Trained model files registered with compliance metadata, lineage tracking, associated workflow runs, source data artifacts, statistical properties, evaluation performance metrics, and model training statistics. [Atlassian Model Registry: Design](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/2066321263/Atlassian+Model+Registry+Design)
- **Metadata per Model Version**: Compliance status, data classification labels (determining storage policies for UGC vs. non-UGC data), data attribution (single-tenanted, cross-tenanted, bundled tenants, no attribution), and deployment configurations. [ML Model Registry, Serving Platform, and Lifecycle Management](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/TCH1/pages/5576561400/ML+Model+Registry+Serving+Platform+and+Lifecycle+Management)
- **Prompt Configurations**: Prompt DAGs, prompt text, contextual data configs registered for experimentation and tracking purposes. [ML Registry - Metadata](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5096215066/ML+Registry+-+Metadata)

### Experiment Design & Evaluation Artifacts
- **Pre-analysis notebooks**: Required before experimentation begins, documenting hypothesis, sample size, and expected outcomes. [ML Launch Review Proposal](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DTIE/pages/3611920350/ML+Launch+Review+Proposal)
- **Post-analysis notebooks**: Required before production deployment, documenting experiment results and statistical significance. 
- **Offline evaluation results**: Baseline metrics, model metrics on hold-out datasets, cross-validation results, and metrics across different traffic cohorts (e.g., MRR, NDCG, precision, recall, F-Beta, MAP, Hit Rate). [ML Launch Review Checklist: Cross Join Nudge](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DTIE/pages/5390652448/ML+Launch+Review+Checklist+Cross+Join+Nudge)
- **A/B test protocols**: Progressive rollout plans (1% → 10% → 50% → 100%) with defined metrics monitoring at each stage. [Production deployment and validation](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/HADES-7668)

### Data Quality & Feature Documentation
- **Feature store documentation**: Features defined in MLFS (ML Feature Store) with online/offline feature definitions, materialisation schedules, and freshness requirements. [MLP feedback from MLEs & Focus areas for FY27](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~63466da3cafc998a91cf5634/pages/7045633174/MLP+feedback+from+MLEs+Focus+areas+for+FY27)
- **Data quality scorecards**: Including data drift metrics (PSI, KS test, KL Divergence), null rates, feature freshness, and distribution statistics. [Drift Detection Metrics](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/agd/pages/6192530763/Drift+Detection+Metrics)
- **EDA notebooks**: Exploratory data analysis documenting feature candidates and data characteristics.

### Training Run Logs & Lifecycle Documentation
- **MLflow experiment tracking**: Parameters, metrics, and artifacts captured per training run via Databricks/MLflow. [MLflow Overview](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/agd/pages/5795994519/MLflow+Overview)
- **Model lineage records**: Full provenance tracking from source data → workflow run → model artifact → deployment. [Dreamcatcher: ML Metadata Domain Model](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5552928221/Dreamcatcher+ML+Metadata+Domain+Model)
- **Training pipeline source code**: Code-reviewed and checked into repository as required by ML Launch Review.

### Deployment Checklists
Atlassian maintains formal **ML Launch Review Checklists** and **Pre-Deployment Checklists** that MLEs must complete:

| Phase | Required Artifacts |
|-------|-------------------|
| Pre-experiment | Project Poster, Design doc, Pre-analysis notebook, Model validation, Feature engineering pipeline |
| Pre-production | Privacy/security review, Post-analysis notebook, Model roll-back plan, Data/feature drift monitor, Model inference metrics monitor, Infra health monitor, OpsGenie alerts |

[ML Launch Review Proposal](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DTIE/pages/3611920350/ML+Launch+Review+Proposal), [Template ML Launch Review Checklist](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DTIE/pages/4818634684/Template+ML+Launch+Review+Checklist)

**Model Onboarding Readiness Criteria** (must be met before deployment ticket acceptance):
- Unit tests passing in Launchpad
- Model latency within KR (Key Result) benchmarks
- GPU capacity estimated and discussed
- Model registered in ML Registry with a link
- Legal/privacy sign-off obtained
- Unique folder naming
- If model update: include endpoint reference

[Model Onboarding Process Improvements](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020a570c71e24c846068af97060212d4544/pages/6855565375/Model+Onboarding+Process+Improvements)

