## 4. Cross-Functional Collaboration Patterns

### MLE ↔ Data Engineers
- **Feature Store Co-ownership**: MLEs define features in MLFS (Tecton); data engineers maintain the materialisation pipelines and ensure data quality/freshness.
- **Data Pipeline Collaboration**: "Feature engineering pipeline source code: code reviewed and checked into repository" — co-owned between MLE and DE. [ML Launch Review Proposal](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DTIE/pages/3611920350/ML+Launch+Review+Proposal)
- **Data Quality & Governance**: Data engineers own data ingestion, transformation, and privacy-compliant pipeline operations. MLEs consume via approved use cases.
- **Tools**: Plato + Socrates + Airlock for data access; MLFS/Tecton for feature management.

### MLE ↔ Product Managers
- **Planning & Scoping**: PM owns Project Poster (planning doc), Privacy & Compliance Review, and model fairness/compliance reviews.
- **Prioritization**: PM leads discovery, MLE leads ML solution design.
- **Experiment Ownership**: PM defines success metrics and guardrails; MLE implements and measures.
- **CSM Applied AI model**: "DS partners with customers and PMs to focus on high-touch customers... MLE partners with DS, PM, and Eng to translate business problems into solution ideas." [CSM Applied AI - The long overdue intro](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/H3/blog/2026/01/15/6327699060/CSM+Applied+AI+-+The+long+overdue+intro....)

### MLE ↔ SRE/Platform Teams (ML Platform, TEAMServe, 3S)
- **Model Deployment**: MLE trains and benchmarks → posts in coordination channel → 3S handles Teamserve provisioning and capacity estimation → TEAMServe provisions endpoint → MLE configures and monitors. [How do I roll out a new L2 model to production](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120201ddfffba6aec4290997f86108f193ad4/pages/6946515361/How+do+I+roll+out+a+new+L2+model+to+production)
- **Scaling & Monitoring**: Platform teams manage GPU capacity, auto-scaling, SLOs. MLEs define latency/throughput requirements.
- **Incident Response**: On-call MLE → Model Owner → HOT (High-Severity Operational Ticket) escalation path.
- **Key Channels**: `#help-ml-platform` for TEAMServe/MLP support; dedicated rollout working groups per domain.

### MLE ↔ Research Scientists
- **Model Development**: "Data Science (DS) focuses on understanding business problems, sizing opportunities, defining metrics and guardrails, designing experiments. MLE translates into solution ideas, implements, owns end-to-end impact." [CSM Applied AI](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/H3/blog/2026/01/15/6327699060/CSM+Applied+AI+-+The+long+overdue+intro....)
- **RACI**: Core ML RACI — Model Development: Core ML (R), Analytics (A), Engineering (C/I). Productionization: Core ML (R), Analytics (A). [Core ML Team RACI Guide](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DTIE/pages/1051522986/Core+Machine+Learning+Team+RACI+Guide)
- **Tight Inner Loop**: DS and MLE kept in "tight inner loop—from problem definition through rollout, impact measurement, and iteration."

### MLE ↔ Security/Compliance Teams
- **Artifact Compliance**: DMP (Deployment Metadata Platform) validates compliance before deployment.
- **Safe File Format Enforcement**: Blocking dangerous formats (Pickle .pkl, PyTorch .pt, Keras .h5) from production. [Enforce Safe File Formats in ML Platform Production Deployments](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/COMMIT-27251)
- **Privacy Approval**: Required for cross-tenant data access, with PD scrubbing and de-identification.
- **Legal Sign-off**: Required field in deployment tickets; must be obtained before approval.
- **AIMS Audits**: Annual AI system re-evaluations, security assessments covering AI-specific threats (prompt injection, model poisoning). [AT-AI-Register-AIMS Objectives-v1.0](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/RM/pages/6709541084/AT-AI-Register-AIMS+Objectives-v1.0)

