## 2. Standard Operating Procedures and Guardrails

### Model Review Processes
- **PRGB (Peer Review Green Build) Compliance**: All ML artifacts must be peer-reviewed and pass through a green build before production deployment. Non-compliant artifacts are blocked. Compliant sources include Bitbucket pipelines on compliant branches and released ML Studio workflows. [ML Registry<-> DMP Documentation](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5156816091/ML+Registry+-+DMP+Documentation)
- **ML Launch Review**: A multi-phase review process covering planning, model validation, experiment design, and production readiness. Owners include PM (privacy review), MLE (design docs, training pipeline), DS (pre/post-analysis notebooks, model validation). [ML Launch Review Proposal](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DTIE/pages/3611920350/ML+Launch+Review+Proposal)
- **DMP (Deployment Metadata Platform) Gating**: Automated compliance validation that blocks non-compliant artifacts from deploying to production.

### Responsible AI & Bias/Fairness Audits
- **Responsible Tech Reviews**: Mandatory review identifying risk of bias within AI systems. Teams use Atlassian's "No BS Guide to Responsible Technology Reviews" to document risks, stakeholder impacts, and mitigation strategies. [Bias Mitigation in AI](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120205eb410d339754170844dc040125b5093/pages/5716665200/Bias+Mitigation+in+AI)
- **AI Safety Filters**: Centralized policy filtering checks inputs against Atlassian's Acceptable Use Policy (AUP).
- **ISO 42001 / AIMS Framework**: Atlassian's AI Management System aligned to ISO/IEC 42001:2023, requiring AI-specific risk management covering model hazards, bias, drift, adversarial risks, and misuse. [Atlassian Artificial Intelligence Management System](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/TRUSTORG/pages/6891693334/Atlassian+Artificial+Intelligence+Management+System)
- **Model Fairness Review**: Optional pre-experiment, optional pre-production (per ML Launch Review Checklist), covering model fairness/inclusive/compliance review.

### Safety Evaluations
- **AI Content Evaluation Framework**: Backend service evaluating content against configurable rubrics (quality, consistency, policy/safety, bias/fairness) both asynchronously and online. [AI Initiatives Overview - MLSE](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~6359788e1cc605b1fd1664ec/pages/6519534158/AI+Initiatives+Overview+-+MLSE)
- **Red-teaming and Adversarial Testing**: Part of the Development & Validation phase per Enterprise AI Governance Lifecycle.
- **HITL (Human-in-the-Loop)**: Designed workflows incorporating human oversight for high-risk AI decisions.

### Data Privacy Protocols
- **Use case approval from Data Governance and Privacy** required for real data access.
- **PD scrubbing, De-identification, MRP, Allowlist** processes for cross-tenant data.
- **Data classification and attribution labels** determine storage policies (tenanted vs. common bucket, per-region for UGC models).
- **Legal/Privacy field** must be documented before deployment ticket approval.

### Deployment Approval Gates
Atlassian uses a **tiered SLA framework** for model deployments:
- **T1**: Minor updates, no GPU changes — fastest turnaround
- **T2–T4**: Increasing complexity, requiring capacity planning and escalation

Approval criteria:
- Pre-launch checklist completed
- ML desk ticket fields complete
- Capacity pre-planned (T-4 week notice for GPU needs)
- Legal/Privacy documented
- Tickets returned to model owner if any criteria are incomplete.

[Model Onboarding Process Improvements](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020a570c71e24c846068af97060212d4544/pages/6855565375/Model+Onboarding+Process+Improvements)

### Rollback Procedures
- **Progressive rollout with defined rollback criteria**: Error rate >1%, p99 latency >2000ms, auth failure rate >0.1%, any credential leakage, or customer escalation triggers immediate rollback. [Production deployment and validation](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/HADES-7668)
- **Feature gate rollback**: Set Switcheroo gate rollout to 0% — traffic falls back to previous behavior.
- **Safe-rollback wrapper scripts** that preserve ASG floor (from Tony's recent work: [OPP-202605-11]).
- **Rollback runbooks**: Documented per-model with version history, training pipeline links, and deployment pipeline references. [abuse-spam-ml Rollback Runbook](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~638868250/pages/2575376973/abuse-spam-ml+Rollback+Runbook)

### Compute Cost Governance
- **Unified cost tracking dashboards**: Core ML pioneered unified compute cost tracking (SSOT for all ML compute costs). [Core ML Cost Optimization Efforts](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DTIE/pages/4913758943/Core+ML+Cost+Optimization+Efforts)
- **Cost alerting**: Automated alerts for cost spikes enabling proactive response.
- **ML Studio cost optimization**: Run-level cost/usage visibility and cost estimates in the Blueprint editor before execution. [Optimize your ML Studio Compute](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/blog/2026/04/08/6772908836/Optimize+your+ML+Studio+Compute)
- **GPU capacity planning**: T-4 week process with shared "Deployment Capacity Tracker" (model name, regions, GPU SKU, estimated replicas, targeted start date).
- **FY26 GPU infrastructure budget**: ~$9.5M for ML training and batch inference ($6.85M Central AI, $2.65M non-Central AI). [FY26 Cost Forecasting for ML Training & Batch Inferencing](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5458899063/FY26+Cost+Forecasting+for+ML+Training+Batch+Inferencing)
- **GCP cost savings**: ~24% GPU cost savings via GCP-first strategy, ~$84K/month currently realized. [Central AI ML - Compute and Networking](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~852563715/pages/6987885315/Central+AI+ML+-+Compute+and+Networking)

