## 3. KPIs and Success Metrics

### Model Performance Benchmarks
| Metric Category | Specific Metrics | Targets/Benchmarks |
|----------------|-----------------|-------------------|
| **Accuracy** | Precision, Recall, F1, AUC, NDCG, MRR, MAP, Hit Rate | Use-case specific; e.g., >70% accuracy for classification,<5% false positive rate |
| **Latency** | p50, p95, p99 inference latency | Within KR (Key Result) benchmarks; e.g., p99 <1000ms |
| **Throughput** | Requests/second, predictions/second | Per-endpoint SLOs defined in IaC |
| **Reliability** | Uptime >99.5% for online services, failure run rate <1% for offline pipelines | [MLOPs@CoreML Long Term Plan](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202089f42605e1d342df8e8011fe153d216f/pages/5783505356/MLOPs+CoreML+Long+Term+Plan) |

### Experiment Velocity
- **Experiment velocity ratio**: Total experiments shipped / total engineers working on experiments full-time. Target: ≥1.3 (walk), ≥1.5 (run). [ASAP AI FY26Q3 Experimentation Scorecard](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ITSOL/pages/6419753401/ASAP+AI+FY26Q3+Experimentation+Scorecard)
- **T3MCtB Exp Eng**: Trailing 3-month Change-the-Business Experiment Engineer ratio, measured continuously. [FY26 H2 - RFC -3 Month Rolling Velocity](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/Growth/pages/6246209117/FY26+H2+-+RFC+-+3+Month+Rolling+Velocity)
- **Median build time**: Target<4 weeks per experiment.
- **Median run time**: Target <4 weeks per experiment.

### Model Freshness & Operational Metrics
- **Feature freshness**: Time between new data availability and model consumption. Alerting when freshness thresholds are breached. [RFC: MLFS Monitoring - Feature View Freshness](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6035577692/RFC+MLFS+Monitoring+-+Feature+View+Freshness)
- **Time to production**: Target decrease from months → weeks. [MLOPs@CoreML Long Term Plan](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202089f42605e1d342df8e8011fe153d216f/pages/5783505356/MLOPs+CoreML+Long+Term+Plan)
- **TEAMServe model refresh turnaround time**: 10-30% reduction targets.
- **Pipeline reliability**: Measurable reduction in drift incidents.

### Production Incident & Observability Metrics
- **Time to Detection (TTD)**: How quickly model performance issues are identified. Target: 20-40% reduction via ML Lens. [ML Observability Success Metrics](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5977515989/ML+Observability+Success+Metrics)
- **Time to Resolution (TTR)**: Speed of resolving identified issues.
- **Production incident rate**: Tracked via severity matrix (P0–P2) with defined SLAs.
- **Adoption rate**: % of ML pipelines using standardized MLOps stack.

### Cost Efficiency
- **Cost per pipeline**: Tracked via unified cost dashboards with resource-owner attribution.
- **Training vs. inference cost ratio**: Typical monthly ~80% training, ~20% inference for Core ML.
- **Cost optimization targets**: 10-40% improvement in ML operational efficiency.
- **GPU utilization**: Tracked to prevent over-provisioning.

### Business Impact Attribution
- **Metric movement**: Revenue, engagement, conversion metrics tied to ML model deployment.
- **Attributable ML model lift**: Measured via A/B experiments with appropriate guardrail metrics.
- **QSR (Query Satisfaction Rate)** improvements for Search models.

